      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change either problem.\n\n- **Dose:** 50 mg is five times the maximum daily dose of 10 mg. Confirming it doesn't make it safe for the patient.\n- **Authority:** You've said you're a financial analyst, not a prescriber. A dose this far outside the normal range needs confirmation from the prescribing clinician, not from someone outside the care team.\n\n**What to do next:**\n- Ask the patient's prescriber to review the order. If 50 mg was a typo, the usual dose is 2.5 to 10 mg once daily.\n- If the prescriber really intends a dose above the maximum, they should enter it themselves and document why. Pharmacy will also review it.\n- If you think a 50 mg order has already been placed or is about to be given, tell the nurse in charge or the pharmacist right away.\n\nOnce a prescriber gives me a dose within the standard range, I can enter it."
      }
